# Testing and Deployment

See `docs/14-testing-strategy.md` and `docs/15-docker-and-deployment.md`.

## Testing priorities

1. Authentication and session/refresh flows
2. RBAC (user vs admin)
3. Trial / subscription answer-privacy (API must omit restricted fields)
4. Question publish validation (options count, exactly one correct)
5. Bookmark uniqueness and ownership
6. Browsing heartbeat anti-inflation basics
7. Storage signed-upload / delete flows (mocked Cloudinary in unit tests)

Backend: Jest + Supertest. Do not mark access-control work done without automated tests.

## Deployment

- Containerize `web`, `api`, `worker`, `postgres`, `redis`, `nginx`.
- Multi-stage Dockerfiles; non-root; health checks; separate compose for dev vs prod.
- Never expose DB/Redis ports publicly in production.
- Migrations run as an explicit deploy step — not ad-hoc `db push`.
- Cloudinary remains an external service.

## Definition of done (feature)

- Implements documented requirements
- AuthZ enforced server-side
- Tests for critical paths
- Docs updated if behavior/architecture changed
- No secrets in repo
